---
import BaseLayout from '../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import CallToAction from '../../components/CallToAction.astro';
import PageHero from '../../components/PageHero.astro';
---

<BaseLayout
  title="Selling a Home in the Wichita Area | Charity Menefee"
  description="Thoughtful guidance for preparing and selling a home in Wichita and nearby communities."
>
  <PageHero
    eyebrow="Selling"
    title="A thoughtful plan before the sign goes up."
    intro="I'll help you understand the decisions ahead, prepare with purpose, and bring your home to market through a process that stays clear and personal."
  />

  <section class="section-space" aria-labelledby="selling-plan-title">
    <div class="shell editorial-grid">
      <div data-reveal="left">
        <p class="eyebrow">Before listing</p>
        <h2 id="selling-plan-title">Focus effort where it can be useful.</h2>
      </div>
      <div class="prose" data-reveal="right">
        <p>Preparing to sell can create a long list of possible projects. The first task is separating necessary repairs from presentation improvements and optional upgrades. Not every dated finish needs replacing, and a large project may not be the best use of your time or money.</p>
        <p>I'll help you look at the home as it is, account for your timing, and decide what deserves attention before it reaches the market. An established Wichita home, newer suburban construction, a small-town property, and a home with additional land may each call for a different preparation plan.</p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section-space section-surface" aria-labelledby="selling-price-title">
    <div class="shell editorial-grid">
      <div data-reveal="left">
        <p class="eyebrow">Pricing and position</p>
        <h2 id="selling-price-title">A hopeful number isn't the same as a useful strategy.</h2>
      </div>
      <div class="prose" data-reveal="right">
        <p>Pricing starts with relevant comparable properties, then considers your home's condition, location, competition, and how buyers are likely to compare it with the alternatives available at that time. The goal isn't to flatten every property into a price per square foot.</p>
        <p>I'll walk you through the information, explain where the comparisons are strong or imperfect, and help you choose a position you can understand and support. Market context changes, so the recommendation should come from current property-specific information rather than a generic formula.</p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section-space section-sage" aria-labelledby="selling-market-title">
    <div class="shell">
      <div class="section-heading split-heading">
        <div data-reveal="left">
          <p class="eyebrow">Preparing for buyers</p>
          <h2 id="selling-market-title">Make the property easy to understand.</h2>
        </div>
        <p data-reveal="right">Thoughtful presentation helps buyers see the rooms, the condition, and the features that matter without asking you to make the home look unrecognizable.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="feature-list reveal-stagger">
        <article data-reveal="up">
          <span>Presentation</span>
          <h3>Clear the visual noise</h3>
          <p>Cleaning, decluttering, handling obvious repairs, and simplifying crowded areas can make rooms easier to read. Curb appeal deserves the same practical attention when it affects the first view.</p>
        </article>
        <article data-reveal="up">
          <span>Photography</span>
          <h3>Prepare for the camera</h3>
          <p>Photography works best when each space has an understandable purpose and important features aren't buried by everyday items. The aim is clarity, not judgment about how you live.</p>
        </article>
        <article data-reveal="up">
          <span>Showings</span>
          <h3>Plan for access</h3>
          <p>Once the home is active, reasonably consistent access gives buyers a fair opportunity to see it. I'll help set expectations for showing requests, keeping the home ready, and reviewing useful feedback.</p>
        </article>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section-space" aria-labelledby="selling-offer-title">
    <div class="shell editorial-grid">
      <div data-reveal="left">
        <p class="eyebrow">When an offer arrives</p>
        <h2 id="selling-offer-title">Compare the whole offer, not only the highest number.</h2>
      </div>
      <div class="prose" data-reveal="right">
        <p>Financing, contingencies, proposed timing, requested concessions, and other terms can affect how well an offer fits your plans and how likely it is to reach closing. A higher price may come with conditions that matter to you.</p>
        <p>I'll summarize the terms, help you compare tradeoffs, and work through your response. The final choice is yours, and legal or financial questions should go to the appropriate professional.</p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section-space section-surface" aria-labelledby="selling-closing-title">
    <div class="shell editorial-grid">
      <div data-reveal="left">
        <p class="eyebrow">Contract to closing</p>
        <h2 id="selling-closing-title">An accepted offer begins the next phase.</h2>
      </div>
      <div class="prose" data-reveal="right">
        <p>Depending on the agreement and the buyer's financing, the period before closing may include inspections, repair discussions, an appraisal, title work, and coordination around possession. Not every transaction follows the same path.</p>
        <p>I'll track the dates, keep communication moving among the parties, and help you prepare for the practical handoff of the property. If you're selling a property with substantial land, the separate <a href="/services/land-acreage/">land and acreage guidance</a> outlines additional items that may need attention.</p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <CallToAction
    title="Considering a sale, even if the timing is uncertain?"
    copy="Tell me what you're weighing, from pre-listing work to timing and preparation. I'll help you build a sensible starting plan for the property you have."
  />
</BaseLayout>
